# Generated Bitburner status/telemetry files, root level. Default-deny
# rather than naming each one: every new automation script (mcp, dnet, cct,
# maintenance, player-activity, ...) writes its own status/log JSON/txt at
# repo root, and three of them in a row (2026-09-01/02) shipped without a
# matching line here, leaving generated output untracked-but-uncommitted
# instead of properly ignored. Allow-list the handful of hand-authored
# inputs that must stay tracked to sync into the game; everything else
# root-level .json/.txt is game output and needs no entry of its own ever
# again.
/*.json
/*.txt
!/mcp_config.json
!/mcp_multi_config.json
!/player_activity_config.json
!/tsconfig.json

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Claude Code local state (permissions, worktrees) — machine-local, not repo content
.claude/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Node modules (if added later)
node_modules/

# VS Code workspace settings
.vscode/

# Out-of-game triggers (generated)
mcp_restart.txt
mcp_dump_request.txt
mcp_objective_override.txt

# tools/bb_remote.py's connection-event diagnostic log (generated, local),
# and the nohup stdout/log redirects used to run `daemon`/the monitor
# detached — same content, different files, all generated at runtime, none
# hand-authored
tools/bb_remote_events.log
tools/bb_remote_daemon.out
tools/bb_remote_daemon.log
tools/bb_remote_monitor.log

# Generated local governance-auditor heartbeat and logs
.audit/

# Darknet canary test output (tools/dnet_canary_test.sh) — appended-to
# result log, unbounded generated output like mcp_status_log.txt; findings
# worth keeping belong in docs/claude-todo.md or a proper doc, not this file.
docs/darknet-canary-log.md
docs/darknet-canary-phase2-log.md

# Bitburner save-file snapshots synced from the game (saves/tsconfig.json
# stays tracked regardless — it's hand-authored, not game output)
saves/*.json.gz
